{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/344993-interest-check-pbp-wraith-the-great-war","id":344993,"title":"[Interest Check] PbP Wraith: the Great War","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-19T12:07:38-08:00","id":344993,"title":"[Interest Check] PbP Wraith: the Great War","content":"So the Wr20 KS is going on right and I've been reading through my small Wraith collection, getting an urge to run or play a game of it but since my current RP is running another game right now so I can't really do it with them right now so I figured I'd see if I could try doing a Post by Post game here.<br /> <br /> Plus some comments by PaladinDemo over in the WtO forums further spurred me on.<br /> <br /> Now I love Wraith: the Great War, from the historical setting which seems completely natural to WtO to the civil war and all the rules for weapons and warmachines of the era to the art in the book so I'm gonna try to run a game.<br /> <br /> I just need to see if there are people interested in play some WtGW.<br /> <br /> My idea is that's its set in Paris on the eve of the Battle of the Somme*, which triggered the 4GM. That also means the Smiling Lord's Insurrection hasn't happened yet but just like the Storm its coming. PCs are all recently deceased and picked up by their Legions, having died some time over the course of the war so far, and have for some reason or another come to live in the Paris Necropolis when the shit begins to hit the fan, followed by Underworld debris and hordes of Spectres.<br /> <br /> *July 1 1916 for those who don't remember.<br /> <br /> For character creation, the defaults of WtGW and you're all wraiths in the Legions and the Hierarchy. If you want to use something from another book, there's two criteria that must be kept in mind, 1) it can't be modern, it has to be something that could exist at this point in time and 2) I have to have the book in question. At present I have the Player's Guide (both normal and Shadow), the Book of Legions, the Hierarchy, the Guildbooks, Doomslayers and Charnel Houses of Europe.<br /> <br /> Once the PCs have been submitted I will randomly chose their Shadowplayers and they will create their Shadows. At present my idea for Shadowguiding is that each update I'll say if the Shadows are active or not and if there's anything special happening with them. If they're active, the Shadowguide can respond after their Player has responded. Or the Player and Shadow can get together and combine their posts together.<br /> <br /> Of course if anyone has other suggestions on Shadowguiding, feel free to say so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T15:38:33-08:00","id":345183,"title":"","content":"Hmm, definitely maybe. It partly depends on how other projects work out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4462-nohwear","name":"Nohwear","avatar":"data: