achments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T11:51:54-08:00","id":358457,"title":"","content":"<i>Thomas Mccabe is a 23 year old from Ashford, Kent in England. Brown hair, blue eyes, 5' 9&quot;, 185 pounds. He is married with a five year old daughter. An author by trade, Thomas' favorite genre is science fiction. He has two titles under his belt; Cavernous, an adventure about life and sentient beings in cave; and Nocturne, a story about an adventurer who finds a world of eternal night.</i> <i>When war broke out he was starting to pen his next novel, while his titles have small cult followings, he wanted to be the next Jules Verne of H. G. Wells. His fatherly duties slowed him, the war brought his work to a screeching halt. He joined the Royal Army to not only to serve King and country</i><i>, but also to gain military experience for his next novel; a soldier waging war against an unearthly force. An alternate view of The War of the Worlds, from a soldier's point of view and the enemy isn't aliens, something familiar yet still foreign. He served as an artillery gunner, his weapon a 26 CWT Howitzer. He served a year until the battle of Verdun. While in his sleep the Germans released their chlorine gas on February 26th</i><i>, unlike most soldiers in the war, Thomas' death was agonizing slow.<br /> When he awoke he found out that he was no longer of the living. He learned that even the dead are at war with each other. He quickly learned about his new abilities and his shoulder devil. He joined the Grim Legion to continue his military experience even as a Wraith. For his novel now has it's enemy, the dead, and each side would be blurred since he wasn't aware of his new state of being. If he survives the War of the Dead, he needs to figure out how to return home and how to write his novel in his current form.</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T07:20:33-08:00","id":359103,"title":"","content":"Not bad though I'm a little concerned about being 23 with two novels under his belt and a wife and child but I'll allow it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T22:33:23-08:00","id":359905,"title":"","content":"I wasn't sure if novella would be impressive. Plus wasn't sure if novellas was a thing back then.","signature":"<hr 